/**
 * Dev-only stand-ins for a finished /api/preview job.
 *
 * The pipeline needs a live store and a headless Chrome, neither of which is
 * available while this page is being built or screenshotted — so PreviewStage
 * accepts `?fixture=<key>` outside production and renders these instead.
 *
 * Four of them, because the before/after comparison has more shapes than the
 * widget does and each one has to be looked at:
 *
 *   light    real screenshot, real catalogue, and a screenshot of the store's
 *            own search finding NOTHING. The common case, and the one the
 *            comparison exists for.
 *   results  the same store where the keyword index does hit something.
 *   bare     `nativeSearch: null` — we never got to ask, so there is no before
 *            state and no toggle; the stage is the Growsearch mock-up alone.
 *   dark     the degraded end: no browser, no products, synthesised storefront.
 *            No browser also means no search capture, so this is null too —
 *            the search screenshot comes from the same Chrome as the homepage
 *            one and cannot exist without it.
 *
 * The homepage screenshot is a 720x450 JPEG rendered from a mock storefront
 * and scaled up by the frame. The frame dims it in the after state anyway, so
 * the smaller file is indistinguishable and keeps this module a sane size.
 * The search screenshots are full 1440x900 captures of a mock results page —
 * the before state shows them undimmed, edge to edge, so a half-size image
 * would be visibly soft in exactly the state the panel exists for.
 */

